⚔️ LangChain vs LangGraph

| Feature          | LangChain     | LangGraph       |
| ---------------- | ------------- | --------------- |
| Workflow Type    | Linear chains | Graph workflows |
| State Management | Limited       | Strong          |
| Dynamic Routing  | Basic         | Advanced        |
| Agent Support    | Good          | Excellent       |

---

🔧 Best Practices

✔ Keep nodes modular
✔ Use formatters for clean prompts
✔ Maintain lightweight state
✔ Add fallback/error handling

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Complex graph design
❌ Poor state management
❌ Unstructured prompts
❌ Too many unnecessary nodes

---

🧠 Interview Answer (Simple)

> LangGraph is a framework for building stateful graph-based AI workflows. Connectors manage data flow between nodes, while formatters structure data before it is passed to LLMs or other components.

